Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### PATCH /api/reservations/5/cancel - ADMIN, rezerwacja już rozpoczęta
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reservations/5/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### POST /api/reservations - ADMIN, 999 osób w sali 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roomId": 1, "participants": 999, "startTime": "2026-12-05T10:00:00Z", "endTime": "2026-12-05T11:00:00Z" }

### POST /api/reservations - ADMIN, termin rezerwacji 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roomId": 1, "participants": 5, "startTime": "2026-11-10T12:00:00Z", "endTime": "2026-11-10T13:00:00Z" }


### Scenariusz audit logu (po seedzie): 1. USER tworzy rezerwację
# @name auditCreate
POST {{baseUrl}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roomId": 3, "participants": 10, "startTime": "2026-12-03T10:00:00Z", "endTime": "2026-12-03T11:00:00Z" }

### 2. Nieudana próba kolizji - 409, bez eventu
POST {{baseUrl}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roomId": 3, "participants": 10, "startTime": "2026-12-03T10:30:00Z", "endTime": "2026-12-03T11:30:00Z" }

### 3. ADMIN anuluje cudzą rezerwację - event reservation.cancelled i [notification] w logach
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reservations/{{auditCreate.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 4. Ponowne anulowanie - 200 bez zmian, bez eventu
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reservations/{{auditCreate.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### GET /api/admin/audit-log - ADMIN
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit-log
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### GET /api/admin/audit-log?eventType=reservation.cancelled - ADMIN
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit-log?eventType=reservation.cancelled&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### GET /api/admin/audit-log - USER
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit-log
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
